  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-24981d36753935de": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-516",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The term “molten” does not necessarily mean that the image was cast of solid metal. Such may sometimes have been made, especially of small size; but the metallic part of idols was usually a thin plating of metal on a wooden image. See note on Exodus 32:4 (#132). Thus the carpente…"
      },
      "c-7a6295f86ab3f3d1": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-515",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Roberts thinks there is an allusion here to one mode of bathing practiced by Orientals, which is to have water poured on the body by an attendant. The Egyptian monuments give evidence that this mode was practiced in Egypt."
      }
    },
